To find each value of $\maroonD y$, we need to take each value of $\greenD x$ and $\goldE{\text{subtract } 3} $.

For example, when $\greenD {x} = \greenD{7}$:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{y} &= \greenD{7} \goldE{-3} \\\\
\maroonD{y} &= \maroonD{4}
\end{align}$

To find the value of $\greenD{x}$, add $3$ to both sides of the equation:

$\begin{align}
\maroonD{1} \goldE{+3}&=\greenD{x} \goldE{-3} \goldE{+3}\\\\
\greenD{4}= \greenD{x}
\end{align}$
